# agent-session board-driver configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env`. The driver reads it from the current working directory.

REPO=owner/name
REPO_PATH=/absolute/path/to/target/repo
SKILL_DIR=/absolute/path/to/skills/agent-session
BOARD=owner/9

# --- GitHub credentials (issue #191) ----------------------------------------
#
# The driver runs under its OWN GitHub account -- a machine user you created for
# it, not yours. Two tokens on that one account:
#
#   - the agent gets a READ-SCOPED token and cannot write to GitHub at all
#   - the driver gets a WRITE token and performs the run's writes itself
#
# The credential is the containment layer. An agent holding a read-only token
# cannot merge, cannot rewrite an issue body and cannot force-push, whatever it
# decides to run. The prompt wording and the PreToolUse merge-block hook are
# defence in depth behind it, not a substitute for it.
#
# There is NO fallback to the host `gh` keyring. All three variables below are
# required, both tokens are checked against a live `gh api user`, and the driver
# refuses to start if either belongs to somebody other than DRIVER_GH_LOGIN. A
# fallback is reached by omission -- an unexported variable, a cron with a clean
# environment -- and its result is a commit or comment attributed to a human who
# did not make it.

# The account both tokens belong to. Not a secret; it is also what stops the
# driver's own park comments reading as human replies and unparking the issues it
# just parked (issue #183) -- a PAT-backed account has no `[bot]` suffix, so
# nothing about the login itself says machine.
DRIVER_GH_LOGIN=your-agent-account

# AGENT_GH_READ_TOKEN: a fine-grained PAT on that account, read-only on the target
# repos -- Metadata, Contents, Issues, Pull requests, Actions and Checks, all Read.
# Nothing else. Safe to keep here: the agent can read this file, and read is all it
# grants.
AGENT_GH_READ_TOKEN=github_pat_read_only_...

# DRIVER_GH_WRITE_TOKEN: not here. See below for where.
#
# The driver also reads a user-level file at
# ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/agent-session/credentials.env (override with
# DRIVER_CREDENTIALS_FILE), loaded after this one so project settings win. It
# must be mode 0600. That file is where the write token belongs -- durable,
# outside every repo, and out of shell history.
#
# Better still, keep only a *command* in configuration and the secret in your
# keychain. Any credential variable accepts a `_CMD` form; the driver runs it and
# takes stdout. The command is not a secret, so it is fine in either file:
#
#   security add-generic-password -s agent-session-write -a "$USER" -w
#   DRIVER_GH_WRITE_TOKEN_CMD=security find-generic-password -s agent-session-write -w
#
# Works with `op read`, `pass show`, or anything that prints a token. Run without
# a shell, so a config file is not a code-execution surface.
#
# What must NOT go in *this* file -- or any file inside REPO_PATH -- is a raw
# write credential: GH_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN,
# GITHUB_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN or DRIVER_GH_WRITE_TOKEN. The driver refuses to start if
# it finds one. A pre-#191 .env usually holds GITHUB_TOKEN, so this will fire on
# the first run.
#
# Be clear about why, because it is easy to over-read: this is HYGIENE, not a
# boundary. The agent runs as you with a shell and can read ~/.zshrc, the
# credentials file, your keychain -- anything you can read. What the refusal buys
# is that the token is not one `git add -A` from being published, not in a backup
# of the repo, and not sitting in the directory the agent is already working in.
# The boundary that would actually hide it is a separate uid or a container, and
# this project does not have one. See docs/usage.md.
#
# Whichever route: a SECOND fine-grained PAT on the same account, with Contents,
# Issues and Pull requests at Write. Two tokens, not one -- reuse a single token
# for both and the agent holds the write credential, which swaps whose account
# leaks rather than fixing the leak. The driver refuses that too.

# Optional: extra logins to treat as machines when deciding whether a comment is a
# human reply. Comma-separated. `github-actions[bot]` and DRIVER_GH_LOGIN are
# always included.
# DRIVER_BOT_LOGINS=dependabot[bot],renovate[bot]

# --- models and budget ------------------------------------------------------

HIGH_TIER_MODEL=
LOW_TIER_MODEL=
MAX_BUDGET_USD=10.0
MAX_ISSUES=1
